  "note": "Brighton’s Pavilion has a ribbed central onion dome, four smaller garden domes, dark concave roofs above the end halls, and slender minarets with open lantern crowns. The east rotunda and end bays have arched lattice screens. A separate domed canopy covers the west entrance. The 10.05 m sea-level datum follows the standard viewer terrain. The plinth extends into the sampled ground and the west floor meets the entrance grade. The cutout covers the original footprint and its mapped building parts while retaining neighboring buildings and paths. Preview places the authored base at the recorded absolute sea-level elevation; local tide and terrain resolution remain host-dependent."
